---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import SectionHead from "../../components/SectionHead.astro";
import TrustStrip from "../../components/TrustStrip.astro";
import CtaBand from "../../components/CtaBand.astro";
import Deco from "../../components/Deco.astro";
import Wave from "../../components/Wave.astro";
import { photo } from "../../lib/images";
import { SITE } from "../../lib/site";

const lang = "en" as const;
const trail = [
  { name: "Home", href: "/en/" },
  { name: "About Ted", href: "/en/about" },
];
---

<Base
  title="About Ted | Children's Entertainer in the Algarve"
  description="Who Ted is: an English-speaking children's entertainer in the Algarve working at private parties, villas and hotels. How each party is planned and what documentation is in place."
  lang={lang}
  path="/en/about"
  breadcrumbs={trail}
>
  <Breadcrumbs trail={trail} lang={lang} />

  <section class="section bg-cream" style="padding-top:2rem">
    <Deco shape="circle" color="#F5C842" size={70} class="animate-float-slow" style="top:12%;right:6%;opacity:.5" />

    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-teal mb-md">About me</p>
          <h1 class="h1 mb-md">Hi, I'm <span class="text-teal">Ted</span></h1>
          <p class="lede">
            I run children's entertainment across the Algarve, birthday parties,
            hotel programmes and family events. This page exists to answer the
            question that matters before you book anyone: who is this person, and
            how do they work?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="blob-frame-alt" style="aspect-ratio:3/4;max-width:400px;margin-inline:auto">
          <Image
            src={photo("ted-com-criancas.jpg")}
            alt="Ted sitting and talking with a group of children at a party in the Algarve"
            widths={[360, 560, 800]}
            sizes="(min-width: 900px) 40vw, 90vw"
            loading="eager"
            fetchpriority="high"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <Wave fill="#F0E4C4" variant={1} />
  </section>

  <section class="section bg-cream-deep">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <article class="prose reveal">
        <h2>How I plan a party</h2>
        <p>
          Before any party I ask the same three questions: how many children,
          what ages, and what the space is like. They sound like small details,
          but they decide whether the entertainment works, relays do not work in
          an apartment, and circle games do not work for thirty children in a
          large garden.
        </p>
        <p>
          From those answers I build a sequence pitched to the rhythm of the
          party: energetic at the start so the group loosens up, winding down
          towards the cake, when children need to be seated and calm.
        </p>

        <h2>Why there is no fixed script</h2>
        <p>
          A prepared programme is only worth keeping while it is working. During
          the party I read the group: if a game is not landing, I change it; if
          one is going particularly well, I stretch it.
        </p>
        <p>
          The rule I never break is that <strong>nobody is left out</strong>. I use
          rotating teams rather than elimination, precisely so no child spends the
          party sitting down after losing the first game. At a birthday party, an
          excluded child is the thing the parents will remember.
        </p>

        <h2>Working in English</h2>
        <p>
          Half the parties I run in the Algarve have Portuguese and international
          families together. I work in English, Portuguese, or both at once. In
          practice the children handle it faster than the adults expect, they
          often end up translating for each other.
        </p>
        <p>
          A lot of my summer work is at rental villas and hotels, so I am used to
          venue rules for outside suppliers and will deal with them directly
          rather than leaving it to you.
        </p>

        <h2>Background</h2>
        <p>
          PLEASE FILL IN: the real background here, when you started, where you
          worked (hotels, entertainment companies, holiday camps), relevant
          training, and how many parties you have run. This is the section that
          carries the most credibility, and the one search engines use to judge
          real-world experience. Concrete, verifiable numbers beat adjectives.
        </p>

        <h2>Insurance and documentation</h2>
        <p>
          PLEASE FILL IN: public liability insurance (insurer and scope), criminal
          record certificate, tax number and registration status. Almost no
          competitor in the Algarve states this clearly, it is a genuine
          advantage, especially with hotels and with more careful parents.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <Wave fill="#2D7A6E" variant={2} />
  </section>

  <section class="section bg-teal">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHead eyebrow="Assurances" title="What is always in place" dark />
      <div class="mt-lg"><TrustStrip lang={lang} /></div>
      <p class="center mt-lg" style="color:var(--on-dark-soft);font-size:.9rem">
        Direct contact: {SITE.phoneDisplay} · {SITE.email}
      </p>
    </div>
    <Wave fill="#F0E4C4" variant={3} />
  </section>

  <CtaBand lang={lang} context="a birthday party" />
</Base>
